WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.320
In the Spring and Autumn period, the states competed with one another and the world was unsettled.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:08.198
Duke Huan, the ruler of Qi, wanted to make his state strong.

00:00:08.548 --> 00:00:11.908
Duke Huan appointed Guan Zhong as his most important chief minister.

00:00:12.258 --> 00:00:15.546
He believed that using the right talent mattered more than anything.

00:00:15.896 --> 00:00:19.328
Guan Zhong had once been at odds with Duke Huan, yet the duke did not hold it against him.

00:00:19.678 --> 00:00:22.798
Guan Zhong pushed reforms, developing agriculture and commerce.

00:00:23.148 --> 00:00:26.316
Qi's economy grew better and better, and the people felt more secure.

00:00:26.666 --> 00:00:30.074
The markets bustled, and the state's revenue grew.

00:00:30.424 --> 00:00:33.472
Guan Zhong also reorganized the army, giving Qi greater strength.

00:00:33.822 --> 00:00:36.774
Qi slowly became the strongest of all the states.

00:00:37.124 --> 00:00:40.364
Smaller states nearby began to draw close to Qi of their own accord.

00:00:40.714 --> 00:00:43.906
Duke Huan summoned the lords of the states to meet and form alliances.

00:00:44.256 --> 00:00:48.024
Everyone acclaimed him as alliance leader, respecting his leadership.

00:00:48.374 --> 00:00:50.894
The assemblies reduced many wars between the states.

00:00:51.244 --> 00:00:54.532
Duke Huan became one of the famous hegemons of the Spring and Autumn period.

00:00:54.882 --> 00:00:57.690
His success came from the power of talent and institutions.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:01.568
So later people often say: to govern a state, first know how to use people.

